module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.PUnit
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Sheaf
public import StacksCore.CategoryTheory.Sites.Cocontinuous.CocontinuousDefs
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.Topos.MorphismOfTopoi

/-!
# A category as a chaotic site, and its morphism to the point

Let `C` be a category, endowed with the *chaotic* topology: the topology in which only the
maximal sieves cover, so that presheaves and sheaves on `C` agree. The unique functor
`p : C ⥤ *` to the one-object category is both continuous and cocontinuous for the chaotic
topologies, and therefore induces a morphism of topoi
`π : Sh(C) ⟶ Sh(*)`.

This is the first half of the setting of Stacks 08PF, the half that produces the morphism of
topoi `π`. The homology groups `H_n(C, F)` that the same tag defines are
`Stacks.CategoryHomology.categoryHomology`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ChaoticSite.pointMorphism`: the morphism of topoi `Sh(C) ⟶ Sh(*)` induced by the
  unique functor to the one-object category.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ChaoticSite.pointFunctor_isContinuous`, `pointFunctor_isCocontinuous`: the point
  functor is continuous and cocontinuous for the chaotic topologies.
* `Stacks.ChaoticSite.pointMorphism_inverseImage`, `pointMorphism_pushforward`,
  `pointMorphism_adjunction`: the inverse image, the direct image and the adjunction of
  `pointMorphism` are the ones canonically induced by the point functor.
* `CategoryTheory.sheafBotEquivalence` is the equivalence between sheaves for the chaotic
  topology and presheaves; it is Mathlib's, and is recorded here under tag 08PF.

## Implementation notes

The chaotic topology is the bottom Grothendieck topology `GrothendieckTopology.trivial`,
which agrees with the topology generated by Mathlib's pretopology of singleton isomorphism
covers. That every presheaf is a sheaf for it is Mathlib's `sheafBotEquivalence`, which is
adopted directly rather than reproved; it applies to an arbitrary category, and in particular
does not require `C` to have pullbacks.

The one-object category is `Discrete PUnit` and the point functor is Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Functor.star`. The adjunction underlying the morphism of topoi is
`sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous`, whose left adjoint is restriction along the point functor and
whose right adjoint is the cocontinuous pushforward; the three specification lemmas say that
`pointMorphism` is assembled from exactly that data, so a consumer may replace it by the
canonical functors at will.

The independent universe `w` in the coefficient category `Type (max w u v)` lets the point
morphism act on coefficients larger than the underlying site, as is needed for sheaves of
rings and of modules.

Tag 08PF is split over three modules of this section, this one carrying the clauses
`chaotic_site` and `point_morphism`. The others are
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/CategoryHomology/HomologyOnACategory.lean` (the
clause `homology_of_a_category`, the groups `H_n(C, F)`) and
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/ChaoticSite/RingedPoint.lean` (the clause
`ringed_point`, which equips the point with a ring `B` and `C` with `O_C = π⁻¹B`).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 08PF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08PF)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07GE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07GE)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe w v u

add_to_stacks 08PF "chaotic_site" CategoryTheory.sheafBotEquivalence

add_to_stacks 08PF "point_morphism" CategoryTheory.Functor.star

namespace Stacks.ChaoticSite

/-- **Stacks 08PF, point morphism (continuity).** The unique functor to the one-object
category is continuous when both categories carry the chaotic topology. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
instance pointFunctor_isContinuous (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    (Functor.star C).IsContinuous
    (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C)
    (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1})) where
  op_comp_isSheaf_of_types _ := by
    simpa [GrothendieckTopology.trivial_eq_bot] using Presieve.isSheaf_bot

/-- **Stacks 08PF, point morphism (cocontinuity).** The unique functor to the one-object
category is cocontinuous when both categories carry the chaotic topology. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
instance pointFunctor_isCocontinuous (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    (Functor.star C).IsCocontinuous
    (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C)
    (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1})) where
  cover_lift hS := by rw [GrothendieckTopology.trivial_covering] at hS; subst hS; simp

/-- **Stacks 08PF, point morphism.** A category with the chaotic topology has a canonical
morphism from its sheaf topos to the point topos, induced by the unique functor to the
one-object category. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
noncomputable def pointMorphism (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    MorphismOfTopoi
      (Sheaf (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C) (Type (max w u v)))
      (Sheaf (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1}))
        (Type (max w u v))) :=
  { pushforward := (Functor.star C).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous _ _ _
    inverseImage := (Functor.star C).sheafPushforwardContinuous _ _ _
    adj := (Functor.star C).sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous _ _ _
    preservesFiniteLimits := ⟨fun _ _ _ =>
      preservesLimitsOfShape_of_reflects_of_preserves _ (sheafToPresheaf _ _)⟩ }

/-- The inverse image of the point morphism is restriction along the point functor. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
theorem pointMorphism_inverseImage (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    (pointMorphism C).inverseImage =
      (Functor.star C).sheafPushforwardContinuous (Type (max w u v))
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C)
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1})) := rfl

/-- The direct image of the point morphism is the right Kan extension along the point
functor. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
theorem pointMorphism_pushforward (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    (pointMorphism C).pushforward =
      (Functor.star C).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type (max w u v))
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C)
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1})) := rfl

/-- The adjunction of the point morphism is the canonical adjunction between restriction
and the cocontinuous pushforward along the point functor. -/
@[stacks 08PF "point_morphism"]
theorem pointMorphism_adjunction (C : Type u) [Category.{v} C] :
    (pointMorphism C).adj =
      (Functor.star C).sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous (Type (max w u v))
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial C)
        (GrothendieckTopology.trivial (Discrete PUnit.{u + 1})) := rfl

end Stacks.ChaoticSite
